{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfxjb9dahKgpEVygCVNhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M8aujcd3g1DKFvvmFrv334","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b/collab/1792330000000-engineer-6b-fix3.report.md","content":"# Slice 6b fix round 3 (opus): F8 regression\n\n**Change (test only):** `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`, new `testing` block \"a closure inside a module store's value naming another module store\", inside `every-store-of-names-a-module-store-of-its-own-task`. It uses the shape from codex's probe and builds it from the harness fixtures. `ghost-fn` closure `g` is routed to `outer` as the result. The module stores are `outer {ghost 1, k <g routed to inner>}` and `inner {ghost 42}`. An authentic stream ref sits in the root store. The test checks:\n- the intact carrier carries both `outer` and `inner`, attaches 1, and `k` (taken from the lowered `outer` store) invokes to 42.\n- With only the `inner` row removed (re-emitted with `rows/emit`), lowering gives 0 attaches and `[:yin.k/unsatisfied #{inner}]`.\n\nNo source changes. No defect found.\n\n**The test bites:** I backed up `rows.cljc` and applied the mutant in `check-dependencies!`, which collects closure rows from `(rows-of (assoc-in task [:slots 7] []) :closure true)`. The quick harness then gave **2 failures**, both in the new block: `(zero? none)` was 1, and status/missing were `[nil nil]`. I restored the file with `cp`. `diff` against the backup and `git diff --quiet -- src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` both pass, and I deleted the backup.\n\n**Verification (JVM):**\n- `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n …safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test`: 51 tests, 1054 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. That is up from 1049; the harness alone has 472 assertions.\n- The same command with `-i :slow`: 2 tests, 706 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- **kondo NOT run:** `clojure -M:kondo --lint <file>` was blocked by the permission gate in this session, so the orchestrator needs to run it. The new code only uses vars that already exist in the namespace (`update-at`, `module-store-ids`, `routed`, `lowered`, `served`, `lift-opts`, `run-beside`, `engine/attach-resource`, `s/ring`).\n\nNot committed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":182,"cache_read_input_tokens":43994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":182},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbd25c6b-20a6-4b41-917b-f6d4b9ac1605","uuid":"efcca977-ae67-40bf-95ca-33158b03d62b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:26:44.505Z","request_id":"req_011Cfxjb9Mxd7AH7pHJ6Zjno","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M8aujcd3g1DKFvvmFrv334":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6b/collab/1792330000000-engineer-6b-fix3.report.md","content":"# Slice 6b fix round 3 (opus): F8 regression\n\n**Change (test only):** `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`, new `testing` block \"a closure inside a module store's value naming another module store\", inside `every-store-of-names-a-module-store-of-its-own-task`. It uses the shape from codex's probe and builds it from the harness fixtures. `ghost-fn` closure `g` is routed to `outer` as the result. The module stores are `outer {ghost 1, k <g routed to inner>}` and `inner {ghost 42}`. An authentic stream ref sits in the root store. The test checks:\n- the intact carrier carries both `outer` and `inner`, attaches 1, and `k` (taken from the lowered `outer` store) invokes to 42.\n- With only the `inner` row removed (re-emitted with `rows/emit`), lowering gives 0 attaches and `[:yin.k/unsatisfied #{inner}]